00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
Speaker 1: We have a really packed program today,&nbsp;
so I'm going to do everybody a favor and not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.200
spend 5 minutes talking about how it's a packed&nbsp;
program and just get into the substance. They're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.840
now trying to ban abortion nationally. I told you&nbsp;
this would happen. It wasn't just me. It's not a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.880
pat on the back. It was very obvious. And many of&nbsp;
us were predicting after the Supreme Court made a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.280
decision which overturned Roe v Wade, overturning&nbsp;
the fundamental right to an abortion in most cases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:32.820
for in the United States. We had this prediction&nbsp;
that this was only the beginning. Now, why was it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.920
such an obvious prediction? Well, you don't get&nbsp;
your biggest win and then stop. I mean, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.260
even Michael Jordan won three championships&nbsp;
before he temporarily retired and then came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.880
back and then won three more. Would have been&nbsp;
weird to just win that first one and then say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:54.180
see everybody later. On the one hand, there were&nbsp;
the sort of more obvious predictions. Well, once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.640
you overturn the right to an abortion, the next&nbsp;
thing is you try to ban it outright. You go beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.020
just overturning it as a right. You say, let's&nbsp;
make this illegal. And then beyond that, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.820
maybe they'll try to overturn the gay marriage&nbsp;
decision from 2015. And on the far end, it's.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:14.160
Well, do they want to try to overturn interracial&nbsp;
marriage? Much more far fetched. But the point is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:20.400
you don't stop after your biggest victory. And&nbsp;
now, indeed, Lindsey Graham has introduced a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.860
nationwide abortion ban just weeks after he said,&nbsp;
well, that's something that should be left up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:30.300
to the states. Lindsey Graham is a hypocrite, of&nbsp;
course, but that's not really what this is about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.440
This is really about the obvious predictability&nbsp;
that this is something they were going to try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:40.020
do. As Rolling Stone writes, Lindsey Graham&nbsp;
introduced a federal abortion ban Tuesday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:45.720
weeks after declaring it's an issue that should be&nbsp;
left to the states. I think we should have a law&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:52.800
at the federal level, says Lindsey, that would&nbsp;
say that after 15 weeks, no abortion on demand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.960
Now, on demand is another one of these propaganda&nbsp;
terms. What does it mean on demand? It's like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:03.660
you could just add it to anything. Well, I don't&nbsp;
know. What about knee replacement on demand? We're&nbsp;&nbsp;

